docs {
  Failure paths. Runs last because it owns a member account from creation to
  deletion and would otherwise leave one behind for the pagination examples
  to trip over.

  This folder spends five of the ten login attempts an IP gets per fifteen
  minutes: wrong-password, unknown-email, malformed-body, as-member and
  disabled-account. The malformed body still costs one, because the limiter
  charges the IP before it discovers the body will not parse. With
  auth/login that is six per full run, so a second run inside the same
  window runs out partway through and answers 429 from login-as-member
  onwards.

  That is a limiter, not a fault. Clear it and run again:

    docker exec goscaffold-redis redis-cli --scan --pattern 'rl:*' \
      | xargs -r docker exec -i goscaffold-redis redis-cli del
}
